## Context

`erg check` warns `regressive log timestamps -- routine after a git rebase
replay; advisory only` when an older-stamped log entry follows a newer one
(src/go/check.go, `logShapeIssues`, added by 0304). On this repo it fires on
44 files.

The spec (src/go/assets/spec-erg-v1.md, Log section) says only "Append-only"
and "Lines are never edited or deleted": no MUST or SHOULD on chronological
order. Append order is the record; a rebase replay legitimately appends an
older stamp after a newer one.

The warning has no legitimate remedy: the only way to silence it is to
reorder log lines, which the spec forbids. A warning nobody may act on is
noise, and it trains readers to skip the warnings that matter. The sibling
"displaced log entry" warning has a remedy that edits no entry (move the
blank) and stays.

Author's request (2026-11-09): remove the noise.

## Scope

- Remove the regressive-timestamp detection and its WARN from erg check.
- Keep the displaced-entry warning and its tests unchanged.
- Update docs/erg-manual.md (the "Regressive log timestamps" bullet) and any
  other mention; add a CHANGELOG line if the project records check-output
  changes there.
- Closed ticket 0304 stays as written (durable record).

## Test

- A file with regressive timestamps draws no warning from erg check (exit 0,
  no "regressive" output); the existing regressive-fires test is inverted or
  removed accordingly.
- The displaced-entry warning still fires on its existing fixtures.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] erg check emits no regressive-timestamp warning
- [ ] displaced-entry warning unchanged and still tested
- [ ] docs mention of the regressive warning removed
- [ ] make test and make validate pass

## Imagine (raid aa12e2)

Verdict PROCEED; premise holds (check.go untouched on log shape since 0304).
Blind-spot: 2 omissions, neither reverses.

- Collapse `logShapeIssues` to one bool (displaced); a never-read second
  return is dead code. Reword the "two advisory shapes" comments.
- Remove the regressive bullet from `helpCheck` and regenerate
  docs/erg-manual.md with `make docs` (tests/test_docs.sh guards drift); no
  hand edit.
- check_test.go: invert "regressive timestamps warn" into a no-warning case;
  drop "displaced and regressive on one file" and "equal consecutive
  timestamps are not regressive".
- No embedded asset, shell test, CHANGELOG or STATE mention.
- Leave tickets/erg to its CI rebuild on main.
- Cross-project consumer: the harness test
  ~/.agents/tests/test_erg_log_placement.py:103-111 asserts the regressive
  WARN; it reddens when the harness syncs this binary. Not editable from
  here: a ticket goes to the harness store, named in the PR body.
- Residual: a hand-edit inserting a line mid-log (forbidden by append-only)
  is no longer flagged by anything; erg itself never produces it, and 44
  false positives on this repo already drowned the signal. Say so in the
  commit message.
